{"created": "2026-09-12T10:18:20.907588+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-12T10:18:21.186729+00:00", "id": 22722077, "conceptrecid": "22722076", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22722077", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22722076", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722077", "metadata": {"title": "Punctured point spectrum of a four-regular bipartite Cayley graph", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22722077", "publication_date": "2026-09-12", "description": "<p>Let \\(G=\\langle a,t\\mid a^3=t^2=1\\rangle\\) and \\(S=\\{a^ita^j:1\\le i,j\\le2\\}\\). The Cayley graph \\(\\Gamma=\\operatorname{Cay}(G,S)\\) is infinite, connected, simple, four-regular, bipartite and vertex-transitive. Its adjacency operator on \\(\\mathbb C^G\\) has point spectrum exactly \\(\\mathbb C\\setminus\\{0\\}\\). We give its inverse as a sum of nine translations and construct an eigenfunction for every nonzero complex number using two-dimensional representations of \\(G\\). In particular, \\(\\Gamma\\) answers Kourovka Problem 15.89 negatively. The graph properties, inverse and complete point-spectrum statement are formalised in Lean 4.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Jayadevan, Achyuth", "affiliation": "Manipal Institute of Technology, MAHE", "orcid": "0009-0008-8745-4078"}], "keywords": ["Kourovka Problem 15.89", "Cayley graphs", "Adjacency operators", "Point spectrum", "Vertex-transitive graphs", "Lean 4"], "version": "1.0.0", "references": ["E. I. Khukhro and V. D. Mazurov (eds.), The Kourovka Notebook: Unsolved Problems in Group Theory, 21st ed., version of 1 September 2026. https://arxiv.org/abs/1401.0300v46", "V. I. Trofimov, On adjacency operators of locally finite graphs, Izv. Math. 88 (2024), no. 3, 542\u2013589. https://www.mathnet.ru/eng/im9408 Author version: https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.01926v3", "V. I. Trofimov, Infinite locally finite connected graphs with countable complements in C of the sets of eigenvalues, Proc. Steklov Inst. Math. 329 (2025), suppl. 1, S250\u2013S256. https://doi.org/10.1134/S0081543825600942", "G. Xu and S. Zhou, Three-arc graphs: characterization and domination, Discrete Applied Mathematics 193 (2015), 200\u2013207. https://doi.org/10.1016/j.dam.2015.04.019", "O. Angel, J. Friedman and S. Hoory, The non-backtracking spectrum of the universal cover of a graph, Trans. Amer. Math. Soc. 367 (2015), no. 6, 4287\u20134318. https://arxiv.org/abs/0712.0192"], "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/Achxy/k-15-89", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "lean", "title": {"en": "Lean"}}], "code:developmentStatus": {"id": "active", "title": {"en": "Active"}}}, "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22722076"}}]}}, "title": "Punctured point spectrum of a four-regular bipartite Cayley graph", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722077", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22722077", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22722077?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722077", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722077", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22722077", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722077/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722076", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/22722076", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22722076", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.22722076", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22722077/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22722077/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722077/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/22722077/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:22722077:kourovka-15-89-paper.pdf/full/%5E